            <stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_74d730f1-3cd4-426e-87ab-442409380fa1"/>
                <stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_64d78a71-70d7-408f-a2f8-1b098fd3a67b"/>
                <stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_157bae72-4bf8-4d9f-b076-1615c07f538e"/>
                </stc:Output>
            <stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_es_rat1"><stc:Content>The 3 configurations (baseline, aggressive regen, degraded battery) were chosen to bound the range-gain claim between best- and worst-case conditions, per DefineTestCaseRequirements; each was run at full and downsampled resolution to support both detailed post-processing and lightweight archival re-inspection.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale>
            <stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-07-24T09:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Simulation Engineer" name="T. Okafor"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation>
        </stmd:ExecuteSimulation>
        <stc:LifeCycleInformation/>
    </stmd:ExecutionPhase>
    <stmd:EvaluationPhase>
        <stmd:EvaluateSimulationResults><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_89d2f79f-36c2-487c-91e5-5ab64d210c68"/><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_36736aee-f3c2-4827-978b-756d615ff066"/><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_dc169e71-9658-41b7-a87a-914dfec92ad9"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_esr_proc1"><stc:Content>Post-processed each run's results.csv for cumulative energy consumption and achieved WLTP range, then compared runs 1 vs. 2 (regen strategy effect) and 1 vs. 3 (battery-aging effect).</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_esr_out1"><stc:Content>Aggressive regen blending (run 2) shows +5.1% to +6.8% combined-cycle range vs. baseline (run 1) across the sampled conditions; degraded battery (run 3) shows the expected range reduction consistent with the SoC_max derating, with the regen-gain percentage preserved.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_esr_rat1"><stc:Content>Directly produces the range-delta evidence needed by DecisionTask.dtmd's EvaluateResults step.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-07-25T09:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Simulation Engineer" name="T. Okafor"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></stmd:EvaluateSimulationResults>
        <stmd:AssureSimulationQuality><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_esr_out1"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_asq_proc1"><stc:Content>Sanity-checked energy-balance closure across each run and compared the range-delta magnitude against the SRMD's validation.computational-model.model-sensitivity-quantification entry's stated 2% safety margin.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_asq_out1"><stc:Content>Quality memo: energy balance closes within 0.3% for all 3 runs; range-delta results are well outside the 2% margin used for hard-constraint decisions, so are not sensitive to that margin.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_asq_rat1"><stc:Content>An energy-balance check is a lightweight, standard cross-check for lumped powertrain models and catches gross setup errors that a plausible-looking range number alone would not reveal.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-07-28T09:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Verification and Validation Engineer" name="P. Lindqvist"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></stmd:AssureSimulationQuality>
        <stmd:DeriveSimulationQualityVerdict><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_asq_out1"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dsqv_proc1"><stc:Content>QA reviewer verdict based on the quality memo.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dsqv_out1"><stc:Content>Verdict: results APPROVED for use in the Gate 2 decision.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dsqv_rat1"><stc:Content>Clean energy-balance closure and a margin-independent result support unconditional approval.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-07-28T11:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Verification and Validation Engineer" name="P. Lindqvist"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></stmd:DeriveSimulationQualityVerdict>
        <stc:LifeCycleInformation/>
    </stmd:EvaluationPhase>
    <stmd:FulfillmentPhase>
        <stmd:DecideSimulationObjectiveFulfillment id="sig-c57efcfac2ba"><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_dsqv_out1"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dsof_proc1"><stc:Content>Compared the approved results against the 4 objectives/KPIs recorded in AnalyzeSimulationTaskAndObjectives.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dsof_out1"><stc:Content>Simulation task objective fulfilled: the combined-cycle range-gain KPI is met with margin (objective 1); thermal/corner-case/battery-aging objectives 2-4 were characterised qualitatively within this task's scope and flagged for deeper follow-up at the next gate. Recommendation handed to the governing DecisionTask.dtmd (extra/org.ssp-standard.ssp-traceability.dtmd/DecisionTask.dtmd) for the Decision Maker's Gate 2 sign-off.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dsof_rat1"><stc:Content>The task's primary, decision-relevant KPI (range gain) is unambiguously met; secondary objectives are recorded as partially addressed rather than silently marked complete, matching this task's own SRMD entries that leave several target levels open for a later gate.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-08-01T09:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Simulation Engineer" name="T. Okafor"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"><ssc:Content><ds:Signature xmlns:ds="http://www.w3.org/2000/09/xmldsig#" xmlns:xades="http://uri.etsi.org/01903/v1.3.2#" Id="SignXMLSignature68EAD4C7"><ds:SignedInfo><ds:CanonicalizationMethod Algorithm="http://www.w3.org/2006/12/xml-c14n11"/><ds:SignatureMethod Algorithm="http://www.w3.org/2001/04/xmldsig-more#rsa-sha256"/><ds:Reference URI="#sig-c57efcfac2ba" Id="SignXMLReference3998F8AD">